  "review_outcome": "approve",
  "reasoning": "All five occurrence IDs and frozen complete recipes retain La(NO3)3 x 6 H2O. Original DSMZ1738/1739 Solution3 and DSMZ1741 SolutionC explicitly use 0.06g hexahydrate per litre of the trace solution; MediaDive5819/5825 recipe[8] identifies compound1586 and the same amount. The original recipes use 0.5mL/L or 0.20mL/L of those stocks, so the flattened 0.06G_PER_L entries must not be treated as final-medium concentrations. MediaDive ingredient1586 supplies CAS10277-43-7; Sigma331937 independently supplies the same CAS, formula and six-water structure; PubChem16211478 has H12LaN3O15 and six H2O in the InChI. The actual existing UNMAPPED0423 owner explicitly records source_id1586, so this is the appropriate owner, despite its lost parentheses. NLM C016534 concept table lines68–74 explicitly associates narrower concept M0313204 with registry10277-43-7; the active concept label is lanthanide nitrate hexahydrate. Thus the precise target is justified by the CAS-linked concept scope rather than lexical resemblance or the broader descriptor. Final C YAML uses that exact identity, preserves historical provenance, marks malformed LaNO33 as REJECTED_LABEL, and retains only the verified parenthesized source name as resolving RAW_TEXT. Root amendment correctly removes the superseded ontology-gap deferral, adds the shared proposal and primary evidence, and retains all publication obligations.",
  "source_context_limits": [
    "This review establishes the supplied solid ingredient, not the form after dissolution or sterilization.",
    "No source supplier/catalogue procurement is inferred from independent Sigma comparison.",
    "Flattened medium quantities and unrelated pre-existing source normalization errors remain outside this identity proposal."
  ],
